"source":"choose_or_skip.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef go(i, n, path):\n    if i == n:\n        print(path)\n        return\n    for v in (0, 1):\n        path.append(v)\n        go(i + 1, n, path)\n        path.pop()\n\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    tokens = raw.split()\n    if not tokens:\n        return\n    n = int(tokens[0])\n    go(0, n, [])\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    solve()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"go(0, 2, []) tries 0 then 1 at position 0, and at each choice recurses into position 1, which does the same. path grows by one value on each call and shrinks by one on each return, so its length always equals how many positions have been decided so far.",
